{"name":"Tongue","hex":"#d1908e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tongue","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A village by the Kyle of Tongue in Sutherland, Highland council area, Scotland .","A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tongue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tongue","blocks":[{"text":"The tongue is a muscular organ in the mouth of a typical tetrapod. It manipulates food for chewing and swallowing as part of the digestive process and is the primary organ of taste. The tongue's upper surface (dorsum) is covered by taste buds housed in numerous lingual papillae. It is sensitive and kept moist by saliva and is richly supplied with nerves and blood vessels. The tongue also serves as a natural means of cleaning the teeth. A major function of the tongue is to enable speech in humans and vocalization in other animals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/%D8%B2%D8%A8%D8%A7%D9%86_tongue.jpg/330px-%D8%B2%D8%A8%D8%A7%D9%86_tongue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tongue","wikidata":"Q9614"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Facies_inferior_linguae.JPG/500px-Facies_inferior_linguae.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Facies_inferior_linguae.JPG/1280px-Facies_inferior_linguae.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Facies_inferior_linguae.JPG/500px-Facies_inferior_linguae.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The underside of a human tongue, showing its rich blood supply","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFacies_inferior_linguae.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Foramen_ca